From 1012a5bf96012512c58549cb14df6c6e5b29cf1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bob <robertramsay78@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:36:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Animate: two joysticks - Moving above, With Fire below

The movement layout is now two top-down joysticks on the left of the
Animate page. Moving: Idle in the middle (click the stick) and the 8
directions round it; With Fire: Fire in the middle and fire + the 8
directions, with a fire button that lights up. Hovering a direction pushes
the stick that way; each direction shows its first frame (faint when it
borrows). Walk / In air / Falling sit under them, then a Test button - in
Test the sticks follow the keys or gamepad and the fire button lights while
fire is held.

The 8 directions are now on simply when any of them has frames (no
separate switch); empty ones borrow from the others and from Walk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BQFSzGarhTTpK2DHf8XzFr
